{
  "comment": [
    "The stable-code ownership report of WP-0.8: every code of `permguard_core::codes`, the one contract document that owns it, how it travels and the class it is answered with.",
    "`contract` is a path under the architecture knowledge base; `kind` is `refusal` (a wire `{class, code, message}`), `denial` (the access gate's `{code, message}`), `reason` (a code inside a successful answer or its evidence), `ack` (a stream acknowledgement word), `log` (a log and metric reason only), `local` (a command-line failure that never travels on a wire) or `unused` (registered and documented, produced by no path yet).",
    "A code with two classes lists both under `classes`; each such code is an open finding of the status file.",
    "`http` overrides the status a class maps to where the wire answers another one today; each override is an open finding of the status file."
  ],
